codex
One material weakness surfaced: the snapshot drift job still lets a compat label waive an uncommitted regenerated snapshot. Because the MCP detector reads the committed head snapshot rather than regenerating it itself, a breaking MCP code change plus a stale snapshot can evade the base-vs-head detector during PR CI; the push-to-main check would fail only after merge.
